-- `&&` inside a helper applied to a draw-bound record, as a list element. It
-- used to be refused (set-valued witness construction failed for 'h') while
-- the `if` spelling compiled: Analysis.isConditional counted only
-- IfThenElse, so the binding of h was not enumerated and fell to the
-- set-witness engine, which has no arm for a list element or a named call.
-- `and`/`or` now count as the case split they are.
-- Task and-inside-list-or-helper-over-draws-refused.
data R = R l::Bool, r::Bool
both h = (l h) && (r h)
main = draw h = R (Uniform < 0.3) (Uniform < 0.6) in [both h]
